public class UploadService {
    private final AmazonS3 s3Client;

    public URL generatePresignedUrl(String bucketName, String objectKey) {
        // Enforce temporary access strictly limited to 15 minutes
        Date expiration = new Date();
        long expTimeMillis = expiration.getTime() + (1000 * 60 * 15);
        expiration.setTime(expTimeMillis);

        GeneratePresignedUrlRequest request = new GeneratePresignedUrlRequest(bucketName, objectKey)
                .withMethod(HttpMethod.PUT)
                .withExpiration(expiration);
        return s3Client.generatePresignedUrl(request);
    }
}

try-catch fallback mechanics:
1. TranscoderOOMException: Video transcoding memory usage is unpredictable. If the worker crashes, the Kafka queue message remains unacknowledged. Another worker picks it up after the visibility timeout. If it fails 3 times, it shifts to a Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) for manual inspection.
2. CDN Origin Shield Drop: Instead of 10,000 Edge nodes slamming the S3 Origin upon a cache miss (Thundering Herd), they query an 'Origin Shield' regional cache. If the Shield fails, request coalescence groups identical chunk requests into a single origin pull.
